<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $363.5 mln April 11.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $363.5 mln April 11.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $363.5 million surplus on April 11 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 11</p>
<p>Exports: $396.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $178 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $566.6 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $421.5 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $363.5 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.844 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.851 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.587 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.199 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $381 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
